## 🚀 Prerequisites

1. **Terragrunt** installed - [Installation Guide](https://terragrunt.gruntwork.io/docs/getting-started/install/)
2. **Terraform** installed - [Installation Guide](https://www.terraform.io/downloads.html)
3. **AWS CLI** configured with appropriate credentials
4. **S3 bucket** for Terraform state: `{{.TerraformStateS3Bucket}}`
5. **DynamoDB table** for state locking: `{{.TerraformStateDynamoDBTable}}`

### Create State Management Resources

If you haven't created the state management resources yet:

```bash
# Create S3 bucket for state
aws s3 mb s3://{{.TerraformStateS3Bucket}} --region {{.AWSRegion}}

# Enable versioning on state bucket
aws s3api put-bucket-versioning \
  --bucket {{.TerraformStateS3Bucket}} \
  --versioning-configuration Status=Enabled

# Create DynamoDB table for locking
aws dynamodb create-table \
  --table-name {{.TerraformStateDynamoDBTable}} \
  --attribute-definitions AttributeName=LockID,AttributeType=S \
  --key-schema AttributeName=LockID,KeyType=HASH \
  --provisioned-throughput ReadCapacityUnits=5,WriteCapacityUnits=5 \
  --region {{.AWSRegion}}
```

## 🛠️ Deployment

### Quick Start - Deploy Everything

```bash
# Plan all resources
terragrunt run-all plan

# Apply all resources
terragrunt run-all apply

# Check outputs
terragrunt run-all output
```

### Step-by-Step Deployment

```bash
# 1. Deploy VPC first
cd vpc
terragrunt plan
terragrunt apply

# 2. Deploy S3 bucket
cd ../s3
terragrunt plan
terragrunt apply
```

### View Outputs

```bash
# View VPC outputs
cd vpc && terragrunt output

# View S3 outputs  
cd ../s3 && terragrunt output
```

## 🧹 Cleanup

```bash
# Destroy all resources (be careful!)
terragrunt run-all destroy

# Or destroy individually (reverse order)
cd s3 && terragrunt destroy
cd ../vpc && terragrunt destroy
```

